/*
Problem: Convert Sorted List to Binary Search Tree (LC 109)
Topic: Linked List / Binary Search Tree / Divide & Conquer

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

The middle node of a sorted linked
list becomes the root of the BST.

Use the Fast & Slow Pointer technique
to find the middle node.

Recursively build:

• Left subtree from the left half.

• Right subtree from the right half.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. If the list is empty,
   return NULL.

2. If the list has one node,
   create and return a tree node.

3. Find the middle node using
   slow and fast pointers.

4. Disconnect the left half from
   the middle.

5. Create the root using the middle
   node.

6. Recursively build:

   • Left subtree.

   • Right subtree.

7. Return the root.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

-10 → -3 → 0 → 5 → 9

Middle:

0

BST:

        0
       / \
    -10   5
       \    \
       -3    9

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

Choosing the middle element as the
root keeps the BST height balanced.

Each recursive call builds the left
and right halves independently.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n log n)

Finding the middle takes O(n) for
each recursive level.

Space : O(log n)

Recursion stack for a balanced tree.

Worst case recursion stack: O(n)

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Fast & Slow Pointers
Divide & Conquer
Binary Search Tree
*/

class Solution {
public:

    TreeNode* sortedListToBST(ListNode* head) {

        // Empty list
        if (head == NULL)
            return NULL;

        // Single node
        if (head->next == NULL)
            return new TreeNode(head->val);

        ListNode* prev = NULL;
        ListNode* slow = head;
        ListNode* fast = head;

        // Find middle node
        while (fast != NULL &&
               fast->next != NULL) {

            prev = slow;
            slow = slow->next;
            fast = fast->next->next;
        }

        // Split the list
        prev->next = NULL;

        // Middle becomes root
        TreeNode* root =
            new TreeNode(slow->val);

        // Build left subtree
        root->left =
            sortedListToBST(head);

        // Build right subtree
        root->right =
            sortedListToBST(slow->next);

        return root;
    }
};
